WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.003
Origin Dossier starts where the character sheet stops.

2
00:00:09.003 --> 00:00:18.005
It takes the events that shaped a runner and turns them into things the table can actually use: contacts, enemies, debts, scars, secrets, beliefs, and unfinished consequences.

3
00:00:18.005 --> 00:00:27.008
The player keeps control. The GM keeps the campaign steer. Nothing becomes part of the game until both sides approve it.

4
00:00:27.008 --> 00:00:36.011
A clinic favor can become pressure. A family name can become a lead. A mistake can become a secret.

5
00:00:36.011 --> 00:00:45.014
A scar can become a code the runner lives by.

6
00:00:45.014 --> 00:00:54.016
The dossier can also feed portraits, scene packets, narration, video, and audiobook versions later, but the mechanics stay in Chummer.

7
00:00:54.016 --> 00:01:03.019
Prose never silently changes ware, money, qualities, magic, legality, or build math.

8
00:01:03.019 --> 00:01:12.022
When ALICE reads approved origin material later, it reads character context, not hidden rules.

9
00:01:12.022 --> 00:01:21.024
Weak media can be rejected without damaging the runner. Strong material gives the crew a person to bring into the next job.

10
00:01:21.024 --> 00:01:30.027
Not a backstory pasted on top. A life with consequences.
